// Both aspect variants of FCSE's settings-page layout, embedded into FCSE.exe so the loader ships
// as a single file. page_assets.cpp picks between them at runtime using the engine's own widescreen
// flag, and magma_package.cpp serves the bytes to the engine through a hooked file reader (nothing
// in Dunia will open a loose file by path).
//
// Generated from assets/fcse.rc.in by CMake. The paths are absolute and CMake-substituted because
// rc.exe resolves a relative filename against its working directory, not against this file's own
// location; CMake writes them forward-slashed, which rc.exe accepts, so nothing needs escaping.
//
// The two .mgb paths are in the build tree, not in assets/: the layouts are built from
// assets/*.mgb.xml by JackAll's mgb encoder each build, so nothing binary is committed.
//
// Unquoted, non-numeric resource names are string names, so these are found with
// FindResourceW(module, L"FCSE_MGB", RT_RCDATA) and there is no resource.h to keep in sync.

FCSE_MGB            RCDATA "@FCSE_MGB@"
FCSE_MGB_WIDESCREEN RCDATA "@FCSE_MGB_WIDESCREEN@"

// The script API (src/lua/runtime/fcse.lua), embedded for the same reason as the layouts above:
// there is no loose file for a player to delete or for an installer to leave stale against the exe
// that reads it. lua_host.cpp resolves it as FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME and hands it to require 'fcse'.
FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME    RCDATA "@FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME@"
